# cosmo's trigger key: let the user at the active local seat open keyboard
# event nodes, so the daemon can read the hold-to-talk key without root or
# the `input` group. Pop!_OS grants this already; Fedora's systemd does not.
#
# `uaccess` is an ACL logind gives only to the active session's user on
# this seat, and moves on a user switch. It must sort before
# 73-seat-late.rules, which applies the tag.
#
# What this opens up: any program that user runs can read raw keystrokes
# from these nodes, as programs in the `input` group can. cosmod itself
# masks its descriptor to the trigger keycode (EVIOCSMASK) and sees nothing
# else (SECURITY.md).
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="1", TAG+="uaccess"
